        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2b415c44-8870-5a59-89f2-830ba9189250",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Savenac Nursery Historic District, Haugan, Mineral County, Montana, northeast Washington, northern Idaho, western Montana, Rocky Mountains\n- People: Elers Koch\n- Organizations: Forest Service\n- Events: Great Fire of 1910\n- Topics: wildfire, historic district\n\nFacts:\n- Savenac Nursery Historic District is located near Haugan in Mineral County, Montana.\n- Elers Koch of the Forest Service created the Savenac nursery.\n- Elers Koch also helped fight the Great Fire of 1910.\n- The Great Fire of 1910 was also called the Big Blowup, the Big Burn, and the Devil's Broom fire.\n- The Great Fire of 1910 was a wildfire in the western United States.\n- The Great Fire of 1910 burned about 3,000,000 acres in northeast Washington, northern Idaho, and western Montana.\n- The Great Fire of 1910 destroyed much of the northern Rocky Mountains, including the Savenac nursery.",
